<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">the curse
of dimensionality.
Moreover, we observe that FasterMSC is highly sensitive to normalization.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since we are expected to put similar points in the same cluster, neighboring points in the space should also be clustered into the same category. The superiority of geodesic distance in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Distances. ‣ 4 Preliminary Investigation on Clustering ‣ Dimensionally Reduced Open-World Clustering: DROWCULA" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is related to the prominence of local structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dimension Reduction</span>.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since we need to overcome the curse of dimensionality while conserving the local</p>
</div>
